# Android Native — IntercomPlugin.java

## Class Structure

`IntercomPlugin` extends `Plugin` and implements `UnreadConversationCountListener`.

Init paths:
1. **Static** — `load()` reads `androidApiKey` + `androidAppId` from `CapConfig`, calls `setupIntercom()`.
2. **Dynamic** — `loadWithKeys` plugin method accepts `appId`, `androidApiKey`.
3. **Resume** — `handleOnStart()` calls `setupIntercom()` + `Intercom.client().handlePushMessage()` on every app start.

## Adding a New Plugin Method

```java
@PluginMethod
public void myNewMethod(PluginCall call) {
    String param = call.getString("param");
    if (param == null || param.isEmpty()) {
        call.reject("param is required");
        return;
    }
    bridge.getActivity().runOnUiThread(() -> {
        try {
            // Call Intercom SDK
            call.resolve();
        } catch (Exception e) {
            call.reject(e.getMessage());
        }
    });
}
```

All methods that touch the Intercom SDK or UI must run on the UI thread via `bridge.getActivity().runOnUiThread(_:)`.

## Returning Data

```java
JSObject result = new JSObject();
result.put("unreadCount", count);
call.resolve(result);
```

## Intercom Android SDK Cheatsheet

```java
// Auth
Intercom.client().loginIdentifiedUser(Registration, IntercomStatusCallback)
Intercom.client().loginUnidentifiedUser(IntercomStatusCallback)
Intercom.client().logout()

// User
Intercom.client().updateUser(UserAttributes, IntercomStatusCallback)
Intercom.client().setUserHash(String hmac)  // identity verification — call BEFORE login

// Presentation
Intercom.client().present()                          // default (home)
Intercom.client().presentSpace(IntercomSpace)        // HOME, MESSAGES, HELP_CENTER, TICKETS
Intercom.client().presentContent(IntercomContent)    // Article, Survey, Carousel, Conversation
Intercom.client().displayMessageComposer(String)
Intercom.client().hideIntercom()

// Launcher / in-app
Intercom.client().setLauncherVisibility(Intercom.Visibility.VISIBLE / GONE)
Intercom.client().setInAppMessageVisibility(Intercom.Visibility.VISIBLE / GONE)
Intercom.client().setBottomPadding(int dp)

// Push
new IntercomPushClient().sendTokenToIntercom(Application app, String token)
Intercom.client().handlePushMessage()

// Events
Intercom.client().logEvent(String name)
Intercom.client().logEvent(String name, Map<String, Object> metadata)

// Unread
Intercom.client().getUnreadConversationCount()  // returns int
```

## UserAttributes Builder Pattern

```java
UserAttributes attrs = new UserAttributes.Builder()
    .withUserId(userId)
    .withEmail(email)
    .withName(name)
    .withPhone(phone)
    .withLanguageOverride(lang)
    .withCustomAttributes(Map<String, Object> attrs)
    .withCompany(Company company)
    .build();
```

`Company` builder: `.withCompanyId(String)` (required), `.withName(String)`, `.withCreatedAt(Date)`, `.withPlan(String)`, `.withMonthlySpend(int)`, `.withCustomAttributes(Map)`.

## IntercomStatusCallback

```java
new IntercomStatusCallback() {
    @Override public void onSuccess() { call.resolve(); }
    @Override public void onFailure(@NonNull IntercomError error) {
        call.reject("Error: " + error.getErrorMessage());
    }
}
```

## Java Version Constraints

- **Java 21 only.** Do not use language features requiring a higher API level than the plugin's `minSdkVersion`.
- Avoid Java 8 lambdas in anonymous callback positions if they cause build issues on older AGP versions.
- Use `Iterator` for JSON array traversal — do not assume stream availability.

## Space Availability

| IntercomSpace enum value | Available |
|---|---|
| `HOME` | ✓ |
| `MESSAGES` | ✓ |
| `HELP_CENTER` | ✓ |
| `TICKETS` | ✓ |
| news / tasks | web-only — reject if received |

## Unread Count Listener

`IntercomPlugin` implements `UnreadConversationCountListener`:

```java
@Override
public void onCountUpdate(int unreadCount) {
    JSObject data = new JSObject();
    data.put("unreadCount", unreadCount);
    notifyListeners("updateUnreadCount", data);
}
```

Register via `Intercom.client().addUnreadConversationCountListener(this)` in `setupUnreadConversationListener`, remove in `removeUnreadConversationListener`.
